item.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;hs-featured-image-wrapper&quot;&gt; 
 &lt;a class=&quot;hs-featured-image-link&quot; href=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/build-your-payment-security-expertise-with-pci-ssc-elearning&quot; title=&quot;&quot;&gt; &lt;img alt=&quot;Build Your Payment Security Expertise with PCI SSC eLearning&quot; class=&quot;hs-featured-image&quot; src=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/hubfs/2026-blog/elearning-blog@2x.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width: auto !important; float: left; margin: 0 15px 15px 0;&quot; /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;/div&gt; 
&lt;br /&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Keeping pace with the evolving payment security landscape requires current knowledge and practical expertise—but finding time for training can be challenging. PCI Security Standards Council (PCI SSC) eLearning gives payment security professionals the flexibility to build their skills and advance their knowledge wherever and whenever it works best for them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Justin.sh is &lt;a href=&quot;https://justin.sh/blog/2026/10/cellebrite-advanced-unlocks/&quot;&gt;reporting&lt;/a&gt; on a confidential Cellebrite document that has been leaked to him:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cellebrite calls it Advanced Unlocks (AU from here on), not to be confused with the &amp;#8220;advanced unlocking services&amp;#8221; they&amp;#8217;ve marketed for years. A &lt;a href=&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20260814034529/https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cellebrite-appoints-shiven-ramji-chief-executive-officer-succeeding-thomas-e-hogan-302850249.html&quot;&gt;press release&lt;/a&gt; from earlier this year confirms AU is a new product for 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[&amp;#8230;]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;According to Cellebrite, AU:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is a &amp;#8220;next-generation AFU vector that is more resilient to Apple&amp;#8217;s OS changes&amp;#8221;
&lt;li&gt;works with Stolen Device Protection enabled, which tightens USB restrictions
&lt;li&gt;is enabled by a dedicated appliance with a stated range (!) of about 8 meters...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;hs-featured-image-wrapper&quot;&gt; 
 &lt;a class=&quot;hs-featured-image-link&quot; href=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/the-ai-exchange-innovators-in-payment-security-featuring-auditsafe&quot; title=&quot;&quot;&gt; &lt;img alt=&quot;The AI Exchange: Innovators in Payment Security Featuring AuditSafe&quot; class=&quot;hs-featured-image&quot; src=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/hubfs/2026-blog/auditsafe-blog.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width: auto !important; float: left; margin: 0 15px 15px 0;&quot; /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;/div&gt; 
&lt;br /&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the PCI Security Standards Council’s blog series, The AI Exchange: Innovators in Payment Security. This special, ongoing feature of our PCI Perspectives blog offers a resource for payment security industry stakeholders to exchange information about how they are adopting and implementing artificial intelligence (AI) into their organizations. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
